import { FilesystemReaderCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> FilesystemReaderCopy = FilesystemReaderCopy {
  summary: "Write UTF-8 using a mode, content string, and Path. Successful execution produces Unit.",
  taskTitle: "Save a report without overwriting an existing file",
  purpose: "Save content containing café and こんにちは to a new report.txt. CreateNew requests failure rather than overwriting if a file is already there. The example reads the content back to check the result.",
  setup: "The imports make effects, fs, and paths available. effect fn report directory: paths.Path -> String defines work within directory that returns the content String when executed. with FileSystem is the service requirement, and fails ReportError is the ordinary failure type. let text names an immutable content value; \\n in the string represents a newline.",
  after: [
    "paths.child \"report.txt\" directory returns Left carrying a path problem or Right carrying the completed Path. |> passes a value to the next function; effects.fromEither turns that result into work. file <- executes it and receives the Path.",
    "The arguments to fs.writeTextUtf8 fs.CreateNew text file are mode, content, and destination. CreateNew is a value taking no arguments, so it has no (). _ <- executes the write and waits for completion. Its successful Unit value, written (), means there is no additional result.",
    "ReportError defines three failure shapes: PathFailure, WriteFailure, and ReadFailure. effects.mapError wraps an original problem in the appropriate shape. deriving Show enables display through show. Because the final readTextUtf8 returns the content read back, report as a whole succeeds with String rather than Unit.",
    "Executing withTemporaryDirectory from main runs report in a dedicated directory and cleans up afterward. effects.attempt captures an ordinary failure as Left problem or success as Right text. match chooses message, which println displays with a final newline that was not part of the file content."
  ],
  details: [
    "Calling writeTextUtf8 does not write immediately. Executing its returned Effect opens the file in the requested mode and writes UTF-8 bytes. Executing the same Effect again repeats the operation. With CreateNew, a second execution can fail because the file now exists.",
    "CreateNew protects an existing file, Replace truncates its contents, and Append adds to the end. Replace and Append create a file if absent. None of these modes automatically creates parent directories. Include newlines explicitly when you want them.",
    "This implementation completes flush and close before succeeding. Flushing sends out pending output; flush or close failures are FileSystemError values too. This is separate from a guarantee of surviving power loss. An ordinary write can leave content written before a failure.",
    "Pass a Path obtained from successful parse or child instead of passing a String directly. Correct spelling still permits failures due to permissions or destination state. Unit also does not report a count of characters or bytes written."
  ],
  comparisonBefore: "TS can also use writeFile with UTF-8 content and flag: \"wx\" to avoid overwriting an existing file, then await completion.",
  comparisonAfter: "Here CreateNew and Path identify input roles, while FileSystemError and Unit identify failure and success values. A stored Effect describes work before execution; it is not the same as an already-started Promise."
}
